# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Clear Point Senior Advisors — Environment variables
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local dev. In production, set these in
# the Vercel dashboard under Project Settings → Environment Variables.
# Never commit real keys.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── OpenAI (Clara production LLM — Responses API) ────────────────────────────
# Used by: /api/chat via api/_lib/llm-provider.js.
# Get from: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys — install in Vercel under
# Project Settings → Environment Variables. NEVER paste a real key here, in
# chat logs, or anywhere client-side (no NEXT_PUBLIC_*/VITE_* variant exists
# on purpose — the browser must never see it).
# Provider selection: LLM_PROVIDER=openai|anthropic (explicit); when unset,
# OPENAI_API_KEY present → openai, else ANTHROPIC_API_KEY → anthropic,
# else 503 → client falls back to the deterministic engine.
# Model routing: VERCEL_ENV=production → OPENAI_MODEL_PRODUCTION; preview/dev
# → OPENAI_MODEL_QA (so QA corpora never burn the production model).
# OPENAI_MODEL_OVERRIDE forces one model anywhere (explicit opt-in only).
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL_PRODUCTION=gpt-5.6-terra
OPENAI_MODEL_QA=gpt-5.6-luna
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# OPENAI_MODEL_OVERRIDE=
# OPENAI_TIMEOUT_MS=9000
# OPENAI_TEMPERATURE=           # OPT-IN only: gpt-5.6-terra/luna REJECT temperature (400); leave unset
# OPENAI_ENABLE_WEB_SEARCH=0    # keep 0 until domain-filter contract is live-verified

# ── Anthropic (Claude Haiku) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by: /api/chat (Zara + Customer Service LLM responses), /api/submit-lead
# (lead intelligence enrichment).
# Get from: https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# Fallback if missing: chat returns 503 → client switches to scripted/regex.
# Lead intel returns null → submit-lead succeeds without intel block.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-api03-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── GoHighLevel CRM ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by: /api/submit-lead (contact + opportunity + note creation), /api/sign-soa
# (audit note write).
# Get from: GHL → Settings → API Keys (Private Integration token recommended).
# HIGHLEVEL_LOCATION_ID is the sub-account ID (Settings → Business Profile).
# Fallback if missing: lead submit returns 500. SOA still issues the PDF +
# hash, but the GHL note carries `ghlDelivered: false` for manual reconciliation.
HIGHLEVEL_TOKEN=
HIGHLEVEL_LOCATION_ID=

# ── Vercel KV (or Upstash Redis) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by: rate-limit, SOA token store.
# In production we strongly recommend Vercel KV: the rate-limit pipeline
# (atomic INCR + EXPIRE) and SOA token TTL both rely on it.
# Fallback if missing: per-instance in-memory Map. Per-IP rate limit still
# works on a warm instance; SOA tokens issued on instance A cannot be read
# on instance B (user-visible breakage). Configure KV before any real traffic.
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
# OR — these names also work (Upstash compatibility):
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# ── Cloudflare Turnstile (anti-bot challenge — implemented 2026-08-15) ───────
# Server verify: api/_lib/turnstile.js, wired into api/submit-lead.js.
# Client token: src/lib/ghl.ts (submitLeadToGHL — covers LeadForm, Smart
# Review, Zara, Clara through the single submit funnel).
# Get keys from: https://dash.cloudflare.com → Turnstile → Add site
# (INVISIBLE widget mode recommended for senior-friendly UX).
#
# ACTIVATION RUNBOOK (both vars required — set in Vercel for Preview AND
# Production, then REDEPLOY; VITE_* is baked into the bundle at build time):
#   1. TURNSTILE_SECRET       (server-only; never client-side)
#   2. VITE_TURNSTILE_SITEKEY (public site key; safe in the bundle)
#   3. Optional TURNSTILE_MODE=shadow first: verifies + logs, never blocks —
#      watch [ANTI-BOT]/[LEAD-AUDIT] logs, then remove it to enforce.
# Modes: off (no secret) | shadow | enforce (default when secret is set).
# Enforce FAILS CLOSED: no valid token → 403 CHALLENGE_FAILED, no CRM write.
# Fallback if unset: layer is off (honeypot + min-fill + rate limit remain).
# QA: Cloudflare dummy keys (docs → Turnstile → Testing) work locally:
#   sitekey 1x00000000000000000000BB (invisible, passes)
#   secret  1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA (always passes)
#   secret  2x0000000000000000000000000000000AA (always fails)
# TURNSTILE_SECRET=
# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITEKEY=
# TURNSTILE_MODE=
